//? Title: Kahan summation: inspect the rounded correction
//? Subtitle: Actual sequential arithmetic, cancellation failures and full streamed repeat experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Kahan summation carries a rounded correction into the next addition. It often
recovers contributions lost by a naive sum, but it is neither exact nor
order-independent. We inspect actual arithmetic on a tiny cancellation example,
retain the original million-one stress test and all repeated-0.1 sizes through
one hundred million, and distinguish represented-input summation error from
decimal representation error. Streaming repeats preserve every update without
allocating an enormous repeated vector.
)

\toc

> Two ones can make a difference

Start with 1e16, add one twice, then subtract 1e16. The first one disappears
from the running sum but leaves a correction; the second update uses that
correction. Every table value below comes from the producing native stream, with
no prefix replay. The diagram shows actual running sums and corrections at each
step.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kahan_correction.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/kahan.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::kahan_trace({1e16, 1, 1, -1e16});
    std::print("| step | x | sum before | correction before | adjusted | new sum | new correction |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
    style.width = 6.;
    for (const auto &e : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} | {:.17g} |\n",
                   e.index, e.value, e.sum_before, e.correction_before,
                   e.adjusted, e.total, e.correction_after);
        d.node(std::to_string(e.index), {8. * e.index, 0},
               std::format("Step {} sum {:.17g}\ncorrection {:.3g}", e.index,
                           e.total, e.correction_after), style);
        if (e.index)
            d.edge(std::to_string(e.index - 1), std::to_string(e.index));
    }
    d.save_svg("build/kahan_correction.svg");
}
```
